+# Official supplements — local mechanics lock 1.3.16
+
+Profiles remain separate: Tales/Kids and Flood/Teens. Official Tales supplements do not create a third engine.
+
+## Local authority
+
+- Tales core rules are resolved by `TalesCore.kt`.
+- Things from the Flood core rules are resolved by `FloodCore.kt`.
+- `They Grow Up So Fast` and `Nossas Amigas as Máquinas e Outros Mistérios` exceptions are resolved by `OfficialSupplementRules.kt`.
+- Gemini/RAG may select an allowed `ruleId` from current campaign context, but cannot supply or override numeric difficulty, bonus dice, automatic successes, extended-trouble multiplier, usage limits, or persistent supplement state.
+- Unknown, inactive, cross-profile, or skill-incompatible `ruleId`s are rejected by `MotorBarbaraFirewall`.
+
+## Persistence
+
+`GameSnapshotCodec` v10 persists the active official supplement and its campaign state, including TGUF bond/stage/once-per-Mystery uses/trust/escalation and OFM chips/saved bonuses/permanent bonuses/Hometown Hack.
+
+## Verification
+
+`SupplementRulesHarness.kt`: 44/44 PASS after final local registry changes.
+Project audits: final_1316, final_visual_asset, product_feature, profile_firewall, static_audit = PASS.
+
+No supplemental mechanic is allowed to override the global Tales/Flood profile firewall.
